  "instructions": [
    "Preheat the oven to 400 degrees Fahrenheit.",
    "Roast the poblano peppers in the oven for 30 minutes, then peel off the skin and chop into small pieces.",
    "Toast the tlayudas in a copper pot over medium heat for 2 minutes on each side.",
    "In a bowl, mix together the roasted poblano peppers, chopped mint leaves, lime juice, and olive oil.",
    "Spread a layer of the pepper mixture onto each toasted tlayuda.",
    "Top each tlayuda with crumbled queso fresco and thinly sliced red onion.",
    "Season with salt to taste.",
    "Serve immediately and enjoy."
  ],
